WEBVTT

00:01.360 --> 00:03.396
Thanks for seeing me
on such short notice, doc.

00:03.560 --> 00:07.872
Not a problem, Charlie.
So, what's the big emergency?

00:08.600 --> 00:11.160
Why does it have to be an emergency?
I wanted to check in.

00:11.320 --> 00:13.470
Well, you left six messages
on my service.

00:13.640 --> 00:17.155
Oh, that was just a liquored up fella
hitting the speed dial.

00:17.320 --> 00:19.197
I got five minutes
before my next patient.

00:19.360 --> 00:21.191
Why don't you just
give me the headlines?

00:21.360 --> 00:22.839
All right, I'm seeing a woman.

00:23.000 --> 00:25.514
That's not a headline,
that's the name of the paper.

00:25.680 --> 00:29.468
I know, I know, but she's different from
the type of woman I usually go out with.

00:29.640 --> 00:33.076
- Yeah? Different how?
- Well, she's a little older.

00:33.240 --> 00:34.798
Well, you really couldn't go younger...

00:34.960 --> 00:37.428
...without having to register
with the authorities.

00:39.440 --> 00:43.592
- I mean, she's older than me.
- Oh, we have our headline.

00:43.760 --> 00:47.639
And I'm confused because
I have really strong feelings towards her.

00:47.800 --> 00:49.870
- Do you find her attractive?
- She's gorgeous.

00:50.040 --> 00:52.076
- How's the sex?
- We haven't had sex yet.

00:52.240 --> 00:55.391
Hold the presses,
we have a new headline.

00:56.440 --> 01:00.115
- Do I have to pay extra for the sarcasm?
- No, it's a flat rate.

01:01.040 --> 01:02.917
The thing is, we get along great.

01:03.080 --> 01:06.516
She's warm, nurturing, supportive.
And I feel really safe with her.

01:06.680 --> 01:09.114
Well, let's see,
you're involved with an older woman...

01:09.280 --> 01:11.157
...who's warm, nurturing and supportive.

01:11.320 --> 01:14.392
You feel very safe with her,
and you haven't had sex.

01:14.560 --> 01:19.953
Now, what male-female relationship
does that suggest?

01:23.720 --> 01:26.188
I feel like I should know this one.

01:26.680 --> 01:27.908
Take your time.

01:29.920 --> 01:33.390
Older, nurturing, warm...

01:33.640 --> 01:35.551
Mrs. Butterworth?

01:35.960 --> 01:39.430
Charlie, this woman you're seeing
is a mother figure.

01:39.600 --> 01:44.594
A mother figure? I said she's warm,
nurturing and supportive.

01:44.760 --> 01:48.594
The words toxic she-devil
did not pass my lips.

01:49.320 --> 01:51.788
My point is, because your real mother
didn't give you...

01:51.960 --> 01:55.555
...what you need emotionally, you're
responding to it in this relationship.

01:55.720 --> 01:58.951
No, no, no. This is not a mother thing.

01:59.120 --> 02:01.793
Now, my brother Alan,
he's the needy one.

02:01.960 --> 02:05.032
He practically wants to sit
in this woman's lap and breastfeed.

02:05.200 --> 02:06.758
And not in a fun way.

02:07.640 --> 02:09.596
- So Alan's met her?
- Yeah.

02:09.760 --> 02:13.150
And he's clinging to her like a tree
monkey, which is really pissing me off.

02:13.320 --> 02:15.675
So you're competing with your brother
for the attention...

02:15.840 --> 02:18.752
...of an older, nurturing woman?

02:19.480 --> 02:22.119
Boy, you're just
a one-string banjo, aren't you?

02:22.280 --> 02:25.238
What do you want me to tell you?
I play the notes in front of me.

02:25.400 --> 02:28.836
I want you to cut all the psychobabble
and tell me why I'm so confused.

02:29.000 --> 02:30.115
I just did.

02:30.280 --> 02:32.077
You're gonna stick
with the mother thing?

02:34.880 --> 02:36.996
Look, Charlie,
I've got my next patient waiting.

02:37.160 --> 02:40.277
If you like, we can make a weekly
appointment and explore these issues.

02:40.440 --> 02:43.000
In fact, twice a week
might not be overdoing it.

02:43.160 --> 02:45.628
No, thanks.
I deal with my demons as they escape.

02:45.800 --> 02:47.711
All right.

02:48.160 --> 02:49.149
So, what do I owe you?

02:49.320 --> 02:51.834
Well, I get $200 an hour.
You were here for five minutes.

02:52.000 --> 02:54.275
So why don't we just round it off
and say $200?

02:56.880 --> 03:00.270
Man. Even hookers prorate.

03:00.440 --> 03:03.591
Hookers don't have to listen to you,
Charlie. Goodbye.

03:07.080 --> 03:09.389
Bye, doc. Good session.

03:18.280 --> 03:21.909
- Hi, come on in.
- Thanks for seeing me last minute.

03:25.880 --> 03:28.440
I think I'm in love
with my brother's girlfriend.

03:42.000 --> 03:44.753
- Hi.
- Hi, yourself.

03:45.720 --> 03:49.508
- Oh, don't you look handsome?
- Nah.

03:49.680 --> 03:51.477
Yes, you do.

03:51.640 --> 03:55.428
- And that shirt looks great on you.
- You think?

03:55.600 --> 03:58.956
- Oh, yes. Very grown-up.
- Well, you bought it for me.

04:00.000 --> 04:01.558
But you should tuck it in, sweetie.

04:02.320 --> 04:03.992
I don't wanna.

04:04.640 --> 04:08.110
- Please?
- Oh, all right.

04:08.600 --> 04:11.672
- Are you ready to go?
- I just need a minute, come on in.

04:12.720 --> 04:16.235
- You remember my son, Jeremy.
- Oh, sure.

04:16.400 --> 04:17.549
- How's it going?
- Hi, good.

04:17.720 --> 04:18.755
- Good.
- Good to see you.

04:18.920 --> 04:20.558
And this is his fiancée, Tricia.

04:26.400 --> 04:29.233
Hi, Tricia. Charlie.

04:30.080 --> 04:33.709
Hi, Charlie. Nice to meet you.

04:33.880 --> 04:35.836
- Mom's helping us plan our wedding.
- Really?

04:36.000 --> 04:38.639
- Yeah.
- You're getting married? Lucky guy.

04:38.800 --> 04:41.951
Not that I'd know. I'm just assuming.

04:42.120 --> 04:46.159
- I'm just gonna get my purse.
- Hurry back. Hop, hop, hop.

04:48.400 --> 04:50.072
So you're getting married.

04:50.240 --> 04:52.151
- Taking the plunge.
- Yeah.

04:52.320 --> 04:54.788
I've never stuck a toe in myself.

04:54.960 --> 04:56.757
Actually, I've never stuck anything in.

05:00.040 --> 05:01.678
Anyway, it's a big step.

05:02.280 --> 05:04.111
Not for me. Tricia's the love of my life.

05:04.280 --> 05:07.113
And I can't believe
nobody snapped her up before I did.

05:07.440 --> 05:10.159
Well, maybe she was just waiting
for the right snapper.

05:12.280 --> 05:14.271
I mean, the past
isn't nearly as important...

05:14.440 --> 05:17.193
...as the future you two
are gonna build together, am I right?

05:17.680 --> 05:22.629
- Absolutely. The past doesn't matter.
- That's what I'm thinking.

05:24.000 --> 05:25.319
Okay, let's go.

05:25.480 --> 05:27.789
Okay, nice seeing you again.
Nice meeting you, bye.

05:27.960 --> 05:29.757
Isn't she terrific? I am so happy...

05:29.920 --> 05:32.275
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
She's a catch, let's go.

05:37.920 --> 05:39.956
Why aren't you studying
for your Algebra final?

05:40.120 --> 05:41.189
Because I don't have to.

05:42.800 --> 05:44.916
- You don't have to study Algebra?
- Nope.

05:45.080 --> 05:47.594
All I gotta do
is get a 67 to pass the course.

05:47.760 --> 05:51.116
Then it's adios seventh grade,
&lt;i>arrivederci&lt;/i> eighth.

05:53.200 --> 05:57.352
Okay, we can cross UN interpreter
off the job list.

05:57.520 --> 06:02.355
But let's get back to the Algebra test.
So you're planning on getting a 67?

06:02.520 --> 06:05.239
Yep. Anything above that
would just be wasted effort.

06:06.760 --> 06:08.671
Okay, we have to talk.

06:08.840 --> 06:12.196
Hey, the blind, one-armed dancer's
about to go on.

06:12.360 --> 06:15.113
- This is more important.
- Last week, she fell twice.

06:15.280 --> 06:16.349
Listen to me.

06:16.520 --> 06:19.273
You know what you call someone
who just skates through life...

06:19.440 --> 06:20.919
...doing only the bare minimum?

06:21.080 --> 06:22.672
Uncle Charlie?

06:25.760 --> 06:26.795
You call him a slacker.

06:27.240 --> 06:30.312
- Whatev.
- Whatev?

06:30.640 --> 06:33.837
Are you now so lazy you can't
even be bothered to finish words?

06:34.520 --> 06:38.513
What's your prob? Won't you be happy
if I just get into eighth grade?

06:38.680 --> 06:41.240
I mean, isn't that
the whole point of seventh?

06:41.400 --> 06:44.119
No, that is not
the whole point of seventh.

06:44.280 --> 06:46.555
And yes, I'll be thrilled
if you're not left back.

06:47.120 --> 06:49.031
So relax, it's all good.

06:50.240 --> 06:52.310
Don't you mean it's all goo?

06:53.920 --> 06:56.275
Holy crap, her arm flew off.

06:57.960 --> 07:00.269
That's gotta cost some points.

07:03.680 --> 07:05.352
Two adults for the &lt;i>Wings of Love.&lt;/i>

07:05.520 --> 07:09.718
- No, wait. I get a senior discount.
- No, you don't. Full price, both of us.

07:09.920 --> 07:11.592
Charlie, you're being silly.

07:12.080 --> 07:14.310
For 2 bucks, let me be silly.

07:16.240 --> 07:17.514
Hey, Charlie.

07:18.440 --> 07:19.429
Perfect.

07:19.880 --> 07:22.519
We're at the same theater.
What a happy coincidence.

07:22.680 --> 07:25.433
Yeah, just like Booth and Lincoln.

07:25.840 --> 07:28.149
Angie, this is my mother, Evelyn.
Mom, this is Angie.

07:28.320 --> 07:30.629
Nice to meet you, Evelyn,
I've heard a lot about you.

07:30.800 --> 07:32.950
Well, there's two sides to every story.

07:33.120 --> 07:36.396
And Charlie's memory isn't the best.
You know:

07:36.880 --> 07:41.271
And considering how you raised me,
it was either... or:

07:42.240 --> 07:43.992
Charlie, don't be so sensitive.

07:44.160 --> 07:46.720
Have you met his brother?
Another drama queen.

07:47.280 --> 07:49.271
Okay, Mom.
Always great bumping into you.

07:49.440 --> 07:52.477
Maybe next time you'll be standing
in front of a wood chipper.

07:52.640 --> 07:55.518
- Enjoy the movie.
- Bye-bye.

07:55.680 --> 07:59.195
- Hey, Charlie?
- Oh, swell. There's more.

07:59.360 --> 08:00.793
I'll meet you inside.

08:01.760 --> 08:03.273
Yes?

08:03.440 --> 08:06.671
- Be careful, that woman is a cougar.
- A what?

08:06.840 --> 08:09.354
An older woman
who preys on young men.

08:10.080 --> 08:14.471
- That's not what this is about.
- Right, she likes you for your brains.

08:15.160 --> 08:16.639
And I love you for your warmth.

08:17.720 --> 08:19.278
Nice yanking chains with you, Mom.

08:21.760 --> 08:24.399
What did I do to deserve that?

08:25.920 --> 08:28.115
- Here are your keys, Evelyn.
- Thanks, Justin.

08:28.600 --> 08:30.989
So, what movie should we see?

08:31.160 --> 08:36.188
Oh, you pick, darling. You're the one
who'll be facing the screen.

08:42.560 --> 08:46.075
Okay, X is minus four?

08:47.800 --> 08:51.793
Great. You're right.
See? See? You can do this.

08:51.960 --> 08:53.712
On the test,
you have to show your work.

08:53.880 --> 08:55.632
So let's see your work.

08:55.800 --> 08:57.597
There's no work.

08:58.200 --> 08:59.519
Why is there no work?

08:59.680 --> 09:03.434
I don't need to do the work. Suddenly,
I can see all the numbers in my head.

09:04.560 --> 09:06.630
- Really?
- Yeah, it's amazing.

09:06.800 --> 09:08.233
And they all make perfect sense.

09:08.400 --> 09:11.392
It's like the equations
are solving themselves before my eyes.

09:11.560 --> 09:14.358
Oh, my God, you know,
I've read about that kind of thing...

09:14.520 --> 09:16.397
...but my own son?

09:17.520 --> 09:19.670
No, I'm just screwing with you.

09:24.080 --> 09:26.514
The answers are in the back of the book.

09:27.920 --> 09:29.433
Good night.

09:30.320 --> 09:33.312
You should have seen your face
when you thought I was smart.

09:36.560 --> 09:38.790
Am I supposed to go to bed now?

09:41.040 --> 09:42.519
Dad?

09:43.320 --> 09:49.589
I still love him. I still love him.
I still love him. I still love...

09:56.000 --> 09:59.151
- You're only punishing yourself. Let it go.
- Easy for you to say.

09:59.320 --> 10:01.629
Your mom wasn't four rows behind you
in a movie theater...

10:01.800 --> 10:02.869
...dry-humping a Cub Scout.

10:06.280 --> 10:10.159
Oh, hey. I didn't hear you guys come in.

10:10.320 --> 10:12.959
- How did you like &lt;i>Wings of Love?&lt;/i>
- Oh, it was terrific.

10:13.120 --> 10:14.519
I thought you'd enjoy the movie.

10:14.680 --> 10:17.274
It's the same cinematographer
as &lt;i>Like Water for Chocolate.&lt;/i>

10:17.440 --> 10:19.590
- Yes. Would you like some wine?
- I'd love some.

10:19.760 --> 10:21.591
Here's 10 bucks.
Go get yourself a bottle.

10:22.800 --> 10:25.360
Gee, thanks, but I can't go out now.

10:26.360 --> 10:28.237
I just put my little boy to bed.

10:28.720 --> 10:31.837
You got a little boy?
Aren't you afraid Jake will eat him?

10:33.240 --> 10:34.912
How do you like being a father, Alan?

10:35.720 --> 10:38.518
Well, you know, I'd have to say
that it's wonderfully rewarding.

10:38.680 --> 10:42.070
And more than a little challenging.
Jake's kind of a diamond in the rough.

10:42.240 --> 10:44.879
Jake's kind of a turd in the punch bowl.

10:45.040 --> 10:47.474
Charlie, that is no way
to talk about a child.

10:47.640 --> 10:48.629
He's not a child.

10:48.800 --> 10:51.439
He's a post-pubescent tapeworm
with a bad haircut.

10:51.600 --> 10:52.919
Charlie.

10:54.160 --> 10:56.913
- Was your divorce very hard on him?
- You have no idea.

10:57.080 --> 10:59.196
I'll tell you who his divorce
was hard on. Me.

10:59.360 --> 11:01.555
- Stop playing the martyr.
- Stop living in my house.

11:01.720 --> 11:04.473
- Here we go.
- You keep saying that, but you never go.

11:05.240 --> 11:08.391
I think I'll just go powder my nose.

11:10.840 --> 11:13.149
- See? You drove her away.
- Oh, I drove her away?

11:13.320 --> 11:15.959
- I'm not the one with the poop talk.
- Poop talk?

11:16.120 --> 11:18.315
You called my son
a turd in a punch bowl.

11:18.480 --> 11:19.595
I said it with love.

11:21.120 --> 11:24.556
Anyway, I know what's going on, and
it's not gonna work. Angie's with me.

11:24.720 --> 11:27.678
- Hey, she's my friend too.
- Well, she and I are more than friends.

11:27.840 --> 11:31.549
- Oh, really? Have you slept with her?
- That's none of your business.

11:31.720 --> 11:35.429
Oh, my God, you haven't.
I was just taking a shot in the dark.

11:36.040 --> 11:38.031
No, that's your sex life.

11:38.200 --> 11:41.351
If you haven't slept with Angie,
it's a level playing field.

11:41.520 --> 11:43.476
- You think so?
- I do.

11:45.320 --> 11:46.594
Oh, hey. What are we doing?

11:46.760 --> 11:49.479
- We're going upstairs.
- Okey-dokey.

11:49.640 --> 11:50.789
Good night, Alan.

11:52.720 --> 11:54.199
Good night.

11:54.760 --> 11:55.749
Hey, Al?

12:04.560 --> 12:06.551
- Morning.
- What's good about it?

12:06.720 --> 12:08.870
I didn't say good.

12:09.840 --> 12:11.717
Hey, why aren't you studying
for your test?

12:11.880 --> 12:14.155
I thought we settled this, Dad.

12:14.560 --> 12:16.915
Turn off the TV,
go to your room and study.

12:18.400 --> 12:21.710
- You'll never learn.
- Hey, hey, I heard that.

12:21.880 --> 12:23.916
- So?
- So I'm an adult.

12:24.080 --> 12:26.230
I don't have to learn anything.

12:27.120 --> 12:28.712
What's bugging you, zippy?

12:28.880 --> 12:30.996
Your blow-up doll
ran off with the pool toy?

12:36.360 --> 12:38.157
Just mind your business and do your job.

12:44.720 --> 12:46.199
Wanna rephrase that?

12:47.400 --> 12:48.389
Desperately.

12:50.360 --> 12:53.796
- Good morning, everyone.
- At least somebody's in a good mood.

12:53.960 --> 12:56.758
Well, I'm not usually one to kiss and tell,
but:

13:03.760 --> 13:05.512
So who's the lucky receptacle?

13:07.960 --> 13:10.349
Do not talk about Angie that way.
She's a lady.

13:10.920 --> 13:11.909
During the day.

13:12.080 --> 13:14.640
But once the lights go down:

13:16.400 --> 13:21.315
- All right, fine. We get the picture.
- Oh, I don't think you do.

13:21.920 --> 13:25.959
She left an hour ago, but it took me
till now to safely zip up my pants.

13:28.240 --> 13:31.073
You know, there are parts of Angie
that could sue Disneyland...

13:31.240 --> 13:33.800
...for claiming
it's the happiest place on Earth.

13:34.360 --> 13:35.475
Oh, go to hell.

13:35.640 --> 13:37.995
- Alan, Alan, wait.
- What?

13:50.080 --> 13:51.957
Hi, is Charlie here?

13:53.360 --> 13:57.069
Oh, for God's sake.
They just drop out of the sky for him.

13:57.680 --> 14:00.513
- Tricia?
- Hi, Charlie. Can I talk to you?

14:00.680 --> 14:02.318
I guess. What's up?

14:02.480 --> 14:05.995
I've made a horrible mistake.
I can't marry Jeremy.

14:06.160 --> 14:08.435
- Who's Jeremy?
- Angie's son.

14:08.880 --> 14:10.996
I thought I wanted to settle down.

14:11.160 --> 14:16.393
But when I saw you the other night,
I realized I'm not over you.

14:17.160 --> 14:21.199
Okay, you understand that I'm involved
with Jeremy's mother, right?

14:21.800 --> 14:24.758
Well, I know, but I don't understand.

14:26.400 --> 14:27.389
You're not alone.

14:29.760 --> 14:32.911
I'm so confused. I just had to see you.

14:33.080 --> 14:36.117
Oh, come on, come on.
It will be all right.

14:36.560 --> 14:38.949
Can I get you anything?
Something to drink?

14:40.240 --> 14:42.913
- Could I have a glass of water?
- Sure.

14:43.760 --> 14:45.830
- Here, sit down.
- Thank you.

14:46.000 --> 14:47.797
Alan, where do we keep the water?

14:51.560 --> 14:53.073
Kitchen.

14:53.520 --> 14:56.557
- Back in a flash.
- "Where do we keep the water?"

14:56.720 --> 15:00.235
Hey, I know where the Scotch is, I know
where the ice cubes are. That's enough.

15:01.200 --> 15:04.351
Okay, let me get this straight.
Angie's son is engaged to that woman...

15:04.520 --> 15:07.159
...who you used to be involved with,
who now wants you back?

15:07.320 --> 15:10.517
Scorecards, you can't tell the players
without the scorecards.

15:12.840 --> 15:15.308
- Yeah, what am I gonna do?
- I know what I'd do.

15:15.480 --> 15:18.040
Yeah, three pumps and an apology.

15:21.000 --> 15:23.150
What? You got another move
I ain't heard about?

15:24.960 --> 15:27.554
Okay, forget about what I'd do.
That woman is gorgeous.

15:27.720 --> 15:30.996
- How could you possibly pass that up?
- Easy. I care about Angie.

15:31.160 --> 15:32.991
Forget about Angie.
You don't need Angie.

15:33.160 --> 15:35.754
You're trying to sabotage
my relationship so you can have Angie.

15:35.920 --> 15:40.835
What? No, no, no.

15:41.200 --> 15:42.189
No.

15:44.080 --> 15:47.709
Come on, look at her.
She's young, needy and vulnerable.

15:49.320 --> 15:50.958
Go fetch.

15:51.840 --> 15:54.832
No, no, it's not worth it. I'm not
gonna screw things up with Angie.

15:55.000 --> 15:57.116
Who's gonna tell her?
I'm not gonna tell her.

15:57.280 --> 15:59.316
- That's not the point.
- Okay, think about this.

15:59.480 --> 16:03.075
In a few years, Tricia will be what?
Twenty-nine?

16:03.240 --> 16:06.915
Angie's gonna be 60.

16:08.840 --> 16:12.389
You're looking at grandkids, liver spots
and a dusty bowl of hard candy.

16:13.120 --> 16:15.918
- I don't like any of those.
- Of course you don't, nobody does.

16:16.080 --> 16:17.513
Go ahead. Do it.

16:19.600 --> 16:21.636
Defile her.

16:30.840 --> 16:33.957
- Here you are.
- Oh, thanks.

16:34.320 --> 16:36.470
Listen, Tricia.

16:37.040 --> 16:40.555
You know how I feel about you.
We had some great times together.

16:41.600 --> 16:45.513
- Remember Vegas?
- Oh, yeah.

16:45.680 --> 16:49.912
- We didn't leave the room for three days.
- Oh, yeah.

16:50.480 --> 16:54.189
Of course, I couldn't leave
because I made you tie me to the bed.

16:55.440 --> 16:57.396
Oh, yeah.

16:57.560 --> 17:00.199
Do you ever hear
from the other two girls?

17:01.280 --> 17:02.918
Oh, yeah.

17:04.240 --> 17:09.075
Look, this isn't a good idea.
You need to go.

17:10.000 --> 17:13.356
But can't we just talk a little more?

17:15.640 --> 17:17.835
If we could just talk,
you wouldn't need to go.

17:18.400 --> 17:22.188
- Wait... But, Charlie...
- Trust me.

17:22.360 --> 17:23.998
Jeremy is a great guy.

17:24.160 --> 17:26.754
And he obviously loves you.
I say give him a chance.

17:26.920 --> 17:31.232
But what if you and I
had just one last fling?

17:31.960 --> 17:33.029
One last fling?

17:33.200 --> 17:37.239
Yeah, yeah, we'll go back to Vegas.
This time, I'll tie you up.

17:38.400 --> 17:39.879
You really need to go.

17:41.280 --> 17:43.271
- But Charlie, wait, wait...
- Bye-bye, bye-bye.

17:46.680 --> 17:48.636
It's not too late.

17:52.280 --> 17:55.317
- You can still have her.
- I'm not listening.

17:55.480 --> 17:57.391
You could do it in her car.
How hot is that?

17:57.560 --> 18:01.235
- I can't hear you.
- It's dirty in a car.

18:11.000 --> 18:15.152
- What the hell do you want?
- What?

18:15.320 --> 18:18.312
Tricia broke off her engagement
with Jeremy because of you.

18:18.480 --> 18:20.630
No, no, no.

18:22.000 --> 18:25.959
- I was good. Honest.
- He was crushed.

18:26.120 --> 18:30.159
My little boy had a nervous breakdown
and tried to drink bleach.

18:30.800 --> 18:32.233
Yeah, but I was good.

18:32.400 --> 18:35.631
Oh, good. Tricia told us everything
about you and her.

18:35.800 --> 18:38.997
Everything? And he was still crushed?

18:39.520 --> 18:41.033
You lied to me.

18:41.200 --> 18:44.715
No, no, no, I didn't lie. I just didn't tell.

18:45.360 --> 18:46.839
It was a long time ago.

18:47.000 --> 18:50.595
And I didn't want you to be jealous
because she's young and you're...

18:50.760 --> 18:54.036
- I'm what?
- A real trouper?

18:54.200 --> 18:55.758
Drop dead.

19:00.240 --> 19:02.595
But I was good.

19:07.000 --> 19:11.232
- Well, you can't say I didn't warn you.
- You did. You warned me.

19:11.400 --> 19:12.913
- But did you listen?
- No.

19:13.080 --> 19:14.149
- Do you ever listen?
- No.

19:14.320 --> 19:16.550
- Are you listening now?
- No.

19:17.160 --> 19:19.913
So you're just gonna sit there
and feel sorry for yourself?

19:20.080 --> 19:21.991
No, I'm also gonna drink.

19:22.600 --> 19:26.752
Oh, come on, Charles. This isn't
like you. Apart from the drinking.

19:27.360 --> 19:30.238
- What do you want me to do?
- I want you to do what you always do.

19:30.400 --> 19:34.279
Pick yourself up, dust yourself off,
call one of your little whores.

19:34.760 --> 19:39.151
Mom, have you ever considered
trying to be nurturing and supportive?

19:40.440 --> 19:43.159
When have I ever been anything else?

19:43.320 --> 19:45.311
Right. I don't know what I was thinking.

19:46.080 --> 19:48.674
Oh, it's okay.
I've had a lifetime of being hurt by you.

19:48.840 --> 19:51.718
At this point, I'm just one big scab.

19:53.880 --> 19:55.518
Where have you been?

19:55.680 --> 19:59.229
I figured since you weren't seeing
Angie anymore, I'd stop by and say hello.

19:59.400 --> 20:02.676
- And?
- She's a really mean drunk.

20:03.280 --> 20:06.352
Well,
as I was trying to tell your brother...

20:06.520 --> 20:09.398
...single women that age
are notoriously unstable.

20:12.120 --> 20:15.556
What? I'm nowhere near her age.

20:15.720 --> 20:18.598
Hey, Grandma, guess what?
I'm gonna be in eighth grade next year.

20:18.760 --> 20:21.320
Really? Is this a move forward?

20:22.560 --> 20:23.629
- Yes.
- Yes.

20:25.040 --> 20:27.156
Then congratulations.

20:28.840 --> 20:31.070
Next stop, clown college.

20:31.240 --> 20:33.071
There's a college for clowns?

20:34.760 --> 20:37.194
Okay. Clown junior college.

21:03.480 --> 21:05.471
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

21:05.640 --> 21:07.631
[ENGLISH]
